    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0469" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg369"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.30/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-24T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 24,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>81. Navy Department has now designated a naval mission to proceed to Peru in
                    conformity with request of Peruvian Government.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d430-f1"/>
                    Head of Mission is Commander Frank B. Freyer. Other members of mission in the
                    order of their rank are as follows: Commander Lewis D. Causey, former Commander
                    Charles G. Davy and former Lieutenant Paul Fitzsimons, the two latter being from
                    the resigned list. They are sailing by steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Santa
                        Elisa</hi> from New York August 25th. All except Causey are married and
                    accompanied by their wives.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
